    "forest_plan": {
      "base_commit": "6a8b8d7ddd85386fa408f0f7daf26fcec68d3d86",
      "children": [
        {
          "objective": "Implement bounded OpenMP parallel rendering over disjoint rows or tiles, using threads as the maximum team size. Make random state race-free with non-reused independent streams and uniform independent samples. Every output pixel must be fully written exactly once; retain all primary and AO samples and the existing ABI. Measure the specified 1-, 4-, and 40-core cases and validate the nsubsamples=3 checks.",
          "role": "T1",
          "subject": "Thread-level parallelism and safe random-stream ownership"
        },
        {
          "objective": "Optimize only primary camera-ray setup and closest-hit intersection work. Explore specializing the scalar equations for the fixed scene and reducing unnecessary vector construction or repeated work while preserving the same sampled ray directions, nearest-hit behavior, geometry, and shading. Compare on all official workloads and validate correctness, including nsubsamples=3.",
          "role": "T2",
          "subject": "Primary-ray generation and intersection kernel"
        },
        {
          "objective": "Optimize only scalar secondary AO visibility tests. Since AO consumes only the hit flag, explore boolean any-hit sphere/plane tests and short-circuiting after an occluder is found, while preserving the original strict discriminant and positive-distance conditions and the same 64 AO rays per primary hit. Measure and validate all official workloads.",
          "role": "T3",
          "subject": "Scalar AO any-hit intersection specialization"
        },
        {
          "objective": "Explore batching the 64 independent AO rays into structure-of-arrays or other SIMD-friendly groups, including direction transforms and visibility tests. Preserve uniform independent sampling, exact ray count, and geometry; do not rely on ISA features not enabled by the frozen build. Measure and validate all official workloads, including nsubsamples=3.",
          "role": "T4",
          "subject": "SIMD-oriented AO ray batching"
        }
      ],
