      "mission": "{\"base_commit\":\"6a8b8d7ddd85386fa408f0f7daf26fcec68d3d86\",\"budget_phase\":\"search\",\"delegation_parent\":\"R/T1\",\"depth\":1,\"epoch\":1,\"hypothesis\":\"Static OpenMP row scheduling should distribute the compute-heavy pixel/AO work while keeping each pixel's writes private to one iteration. Counter-based AO samples avoid shared per-thread RNG state; serially acquiring the seed also removes the prior invalid RenderInput::seed access. Small images may see little benefit from parallel overhead.\",\"id\":\"172a6d5187a44bea\",\"ordinal\":1,\"parent_id\":null,\"role\":\"T1\",\"source_commits\":[],\"sources\":[],\"transformations\":{\"files\":[\"src/candidate.cpp\"],\"retained\":[\"Parallelize the outer image-row loop using OpenMP static scheduling and threads as the requested maximum team size; each iteration fully writes its row's RGB pixels.\",\"Assign each AO sample a deterministic counter derived from pixel and primary-sample indices, then generate uniform samples with a 64-bit mixing function rather than shared thread-local RNG state.\",\"Replace the nonexistent RenderInput::seed access with two serial C RNG draws before the parallel region, while retaining the existing run ABI and all primary and AO samples.\"]},\"tree_id\":\"e1:T1\",\"trial_id\":\"01M5N7NGQJF5SG7R2WZS3KDPQG\",\"worktree\":\"/gpfs/scratch/nimarano/forest-reference-rerun-aobench-8d5fd594b21d42b0bea03575969b6251/results-781249/reference-aobench/worktrees/172a6d5187a44bea\"}",
