      "mission": "{\"base_commit\":\"6a8b8d7ddd85386fa408f0f7daf26fcec68d3d86\",\"budget_phase\":\"search\",\"delegation_parent\":\"R/T3\",\"depth\":1,\"epoch\":1,\"hypothesis\":\"AO visibility currently computes and stores nearest-hit intersection payloads even though it only consumes a hit flag. Dedicated scalar boolean tests can preserve the same strict discriminant, near-root positive-distance test, plane parallel threshold, and initial 1.0e+17f distance bound while avoiding payload work. Stopping sphere tests at the first occluder should avoid later primitive tests without changing the 64 AO rays or random-number consumption per primary hit.\",\"id\":\"07ea8c79b0f542f1\",\"ordinal\":1,\"parent_id\":null,\"role\":\"T3\",\"source_commits\":[],\"sources\":[],\"transformations\":{\"files\":[\"src/candidate.cpp\"],\"retained\":[\"Added dedicated boolean sphere and plane AO visibility tests that preserve the original strict discriminant, positive near-root distance, plane parallel threshold, and initial distance cutoff.\",\"Short-circuited secondary sphere checks and skipped the plane test after an occluder is found; retained the existing 8-by-8 AO sampling loops and random draws.\"]},\"tree_id\":\"e1:T3\",\"trial_id\":\"01M5N7NGSB6W9AS0W4FWQFAQ4P\",\"worktree\":\"/gpfs/scratch/nimarano/forest-reference-rerun-aobench-8d5fd594b21d42b0bea03575969b6251/results-781249/reference-aobench/worktrees/07ea8c79b0f542f1\"}",
